  "metric": "Every remaining constant of the fit and of the pattern readout, fixed on training documents only.",
  "notes": "Every number here comes from training documents only. No held-out number exists yet. The training totals hold the seven wrap widths 20 through 140 only, so this strength search is pooled over exactly those seven widths. The readout chosen by this cross-validation is recorded and is not the run's chosen readout. The design chooses that on held-out documents, in the next stage. The label window at a probe window ends at that width, which is what makes the comparison across windows a comparison of probe windows. The window's low end can sit above 1, because the first column of a line needs a one-character opening token and is thin. How far above 1 is recorded per window. A character label enters a window only if training text carries it often enough that the held-out text, a third the size, is very unlikely to leave it empty. An empty held-out label has no average vector, so the character reading would halt and the token reading would be recorded as not computable. The token ceiling is committed by correction 3 of the design: at least 40 training positions. The ceiling is recorded above beside the observed maximum token count and the number of counts the cut removed, so the cut is visible. The previous rung applied the same 40 without stating the rule. The profile length is committed by the design as the label count minus 20. The design also states it as 120, 180 and 260. Both are checked, and a disagreement halts rather than picking one. There is no search band. The statistic ranges over every whole number of cycles whose period is at least 4 and at most the profile length. That range is applied in each labelling's own units, so the token control searches token periods. The fold split and every shuffle stream derive from the one committed base seed, 0, with a separate stream per probe window and labelling. That is the gate record's answer 4, and the values are recorded above. Whether the chosen strength sits inside the grid rather than at an end is recorded above. No levelling-off is required. A further run of this script on the same box is a rerun of the same instrument, not a replication.",
